{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787681465744344768,"compiled_state":{"alias":"shimmery-customary-dorking","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"c8fdab1eac11bb3250e7c79cc19f57deb72411566e62929ccb2c8bcd9b24d099","event_uuid":"c86e031a-763d-42e5-8338-be3ab983aa71","position":{"commit_sha":"0699aa668a7133428c9cc93325681c12e7456288","position":"1787678967773233001-c86e031a-763d-42e5-8338-be3ab983aa71"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"540b00cecf42738619edde435fb4a0f571d92d6c5cf2eb492a0b9e5590020620","event_uuid":"b249272b-84af-4d38-8378-c4bf8b7178f1","position":{"commit_sha":"f6898a47251a85fe2410c5f11e15eb6bc1142afa","position":"1787679010138793001-b249272b-84af-4d38-8378-c4bf8b7178f1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"95aaed1206c00e6c52152e413655bcfdf2f8f7b8137b071b209520970edb781f","event_uuid":"22f2c8fe-5781-408e-8762-992be538042b","position":{"commit_sha":"e1c9c98fbbc367206913a468489e46623388e964","position":"1787679341566168001-22f2c8fe-5781-408e-8762-992be538042b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787678967773233001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b249272b-84af-4d38-8378-c4bf8b7178f1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"99cd-e61b-bc64-48af"},{"link_uuid":"22f2c8fe-5781-408e-8762-992be538042b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b03c-f8d4-ef82-4618"}],"description":"## Suspected defect\nA source-path audit at code revision d49466b5e960 suggests that one completion operation may combine code evidence read from the immutable tree selected by `--ref` with prefetch, deterministic checks, or later signing inputs rooted at the live checkout. This is a hypothesis from control-flow inspection, not a demonstrated failure. It MUST be verified experimentally before any production change.\n\nThe public contract is that checks which judge the implementation are based on the code revision supplied by `--ref`. Comparisons against live state can be valid for drift detection, ancestry, optimistic concurrency, or publication safety, but live checkout content must not become verdict evidence for a `--ref`-targeted run.\n\n## Mandatory reproduction before remediation\n1. Build a disposable Git fixture with revisions A and B whose source, referencing commit evidence, and a prefetched file deliberately disagree. Keep the live checkout at B and invoke the real completion path with `--ref A`.\n2. Instrument or spy on every code-root/ref input used by context assembly, completion prefetch, deterministic commit/file checks, verifier tools, drift checks, and completion-signature material. Record the resolved OID and classify each read as verdict evidence, ticket-state evidence, or an intentional live-state comparison.\n3. Prove whether all verdict-bearing code reads resolve to A. If they do, record the falsification and close this bug without a speculative refactor. If any verdict-bearing read resolves to B, preserve the failing experiment as the regression test before changing code.\n\n## Remediation constraints if reproduced\n- Thread one explicit pinned-code handle/OID through every verdict-bearing path; do not let a generic `repo_root` silently select live code.\n- Keep intentional live comparisons explicit and one-way: they may reject/retry stale work, but may not contribute evidence that makes a criterion pass or fail.\n- Bind `verified_at_sha` and the completion signature to the same A selected by `--ref`.\n- Cover a moving branch name as well as a concrete SHA, resolving the name once at operation start.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic divergent-A/B experiment proves or falsifies the suspected mixed-root behavior through the real completion orchestration path.\n- [ ] The evidence records the resolved OID and purpose of every code read used by prefetch, deterministic checks, agent file tools, drift comparison, and signing.\n- [ ] If reproduced, a regression test fails before the fix when live=B and `--ref=A`, then passes only when every verdict-bearing check uses A.\n- [ ] Intentional live-state comparisons are named and tested to fail closed or retry without becoming verdict evidence.\n- [ ] The emitted `verified_at_sha` and signed completion manifest equal A.\n- [ ] If the experiment falsifies the hypothesis, no production behavior is changed and the ticket closes with the falsifying evidence.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","b03c-f8d4-ef82-4618"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["completion-verifier","pinned-ref","correctness","experiment-first"],"ticket_id":"831f-326d-be85-437a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"--ref-targeted completion may mix pinned code with live-checkout inputs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c86e031a-763d-42e5-8338-be3ab983aa71","b249272b-84af-4d38-8378-c4bf8b7178f1","22f2c8fe-5781-408e-8762-992be538042b"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787681465744344768,"uuid":"effff0d6-7419-4ea6-ad98-d2bf1b21ad38"}